Description": "The global energy, services, and commodities company\u2014which provides fuel to planes, boats, and trucks\u2014impressed Wall Street with its earnings results all four quarters last year. World Fuel Services, led by CEO Michael Kasbar, generated $36.8 billion in profit on $178.9 billion in revenue in 2019. Though revenue was down 7.4% from 2018, partially due to lower fuel prices across business lines, profits increased by 40% year over year thanks to careful managment of costs. Today, during a global pandemic in which the company's aviation business has been severely impacted, World Fuel's management maintains it can once again reduce expenses and manage its cash through the crisis."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 91, "itemDescription": "The global energy, services, and commodities company\u2014which provides fuel to planes, boats, and trucks\u2014impressed Wall Street with its earnings results all four quarters last year. World Fuel Services, led by CEO Michael Kasbar, generated $36.8 billion in profit on $178.9 billion in revenue in 2019. Though revenue was down 7.4% from 2018, partially due to lower fuel prices across business lines, profits increased by 40% year over year thanks to careful managment of costs. Today, during a global pandemic when the company's aviation business is severely impacted, leadership says it can once again reduce expenses and manage its cash through the crisis."}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 309, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 83, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 351, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 91, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2017, "rank": null, "itemDescri